// ---- S1 sparkline axis for the haircut tooltip: 12 steps, 1 = 11 months before the as-of month ... 12 = as-of month.
//      Modeling ▸ New table ▸ paste ▸ Enter. No relationship. Hide Label if you like (Step is the axis).
P6W HC Month =
SELECTCOLUMNS ( GENERATESERIES ( 1, 12, 1 ), "Step", [Value], "Label", "m-" & ( 12 - [Value] ) )

// ---- S2 Movers detail switch = a FIELD PARAMETER (Modeling ▸ New parameter ▸ Fields). Do NOT paste with New table.
// Name: P6W M Detail. Add, in this order: _Measures ▸ P6 M Blank, then DIM_COUNTERPARTY ▸ CPY Label. Untick "Add slicer".
// In the formula bar change only the two labels to CPH / CPY, so it reads:
//
// P6W M Detail = {
//     ( "CPH", NAMEOF ( '_Measures'[P6 M Blank] ), 0 ),
//     ( "CPY", NAMEOF ( 'DIM_COUNTERPARTY'[CPY Label] ), 1 )
// }
//
// "CPH" = the Movers table as today (the blank measure adds an empty, zero-width column); "CPY" = the CPYs of each CPH
// listed under it. Nothing else changes.
